# Automated CI/CD Publishing Pipeline Configuration

## Workflow Architecture Overview
Every pull request targeting the production documentation repository triggers an automated validation pipeline via GitHub Actions. Content cannot be merged into the production branch until all automated code quality gates pass successfully.

```text
[Commit Pushed] ──> [Lint Checks] ──> [Link Validator] ──> [Build Dry-Run] ──> [Staging Deploy]
```

## GitHub Actions Workflow Configuration Matrix
Below is the system file defining our automated compilation gates (`.github/workflows/docs-deploy.yml`):

```yaml
name: Deploy Documentation

on:
  push:
    branches:
      - main # Triggers when code is pushed to the main branch

# Sets permissions of the GITHUB_TOKEN to allow deployment to GitHub Pages
permissions:
  contents: read
  pages: write
  id-token: write

# Allow only one concurrent deployment, skipping runs queued between the run in-progress and latest queued.
# However, do NOT cancel in-progress runs as we want to allow these production deployments to complete.
concurrency:
  group: "pages"
  cancel-in-progress: false

jobs:
  deploy:
    environment:
      name: github-pages
      url: ${{ steps:deployment.outputs.page_url }}
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - name: Checkout Repository
        uses: actions/checkout@v4

      # OPTIONAL: Insert documentation build tools here if needed (e.g., MkDocs, Sphinx, Docusaurus, npm run build)
      # Example for a Node-based SSG:
      # - name: Setup Node.js
      #   uses: actions/setup-node@v4
      #   with:
      #     node-version: '20'
      # - name: Install Dependencies & Build
      #   run: |
      #     npm ci
      #     npm run build

      - name: Setup Pages
        uses: actions/configure-pages@v5

      - name: Upload Artifact
        uses: actions/upload-pages-artifact@v3
        with:
          # Point this to your built documentation folder (e.g., './dist', './site', or './' if it's raw HTML)
          path: './docs'

      - name: Deploy to GitHub Pages
        id: deployment
        uses: actions/deploy-pages@v4
```

